{:edb/db-before-t 1178 :edb/db-after-t 1179 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534491 50 #inst "2026-10-07T08:42:38.957Z" 13194139534491 true] [17592186064131 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291719 13194139534491 true] [17592186064132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291726 13194139534491 true] [17592186064132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291729 13194139534491 true] [17592186064162 1020 #edb/ref 17592186291742 13194139534491 true] [17592186064851 1017 #edb/ref 17592186063616 13194139534491 false] [17592186064851 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291736 13194139534491 true] [17592186064851 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534491 true] [17592186064851 1100 "$\\int \\frac{8\\,\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}=$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186064851 1100 "What is $∫(8dx)/(\\mid 8x \\mid \\sqrt{(8x)^{2} - 1})$?" 13194139534491 false] [17592186064851 1145 "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8\\,\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}=8\\int \\frac{\\text{d}x}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nThis integral now resembles the basic one for $\\text{arcsec},$\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\text{d}u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $8x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=8x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=8\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}8\\int \\frac{1}{|8x|\\sqrt{(8x)^{2}-1}}\\text{d}x & =8\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{8}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(8x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291719 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291720 13194139534491 true] [17592186291719 1089 "q-114035" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291719 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534491 true] [17592186291719 1100 "Calculate $\\int \\frac{1}{1+5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291719 1113 #uuid "7e87ee1c-de87-5e56-a6b4-aa28a90fdbbc" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291719 1145 "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $5{x}^{2}=(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}.$\n\nThus, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{5}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{1+5{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291721 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291722 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291723 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291724 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291725 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1041 "selection" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291721 13194139534491 true] [17592186291720 1110 #uuid "7c120401-7883-54dd-aec7-28ba54869b16" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291721 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291721 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291721 1111 #uuid "89cf2c27-6756-5ca7-831a-9d6ee9325cf2" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291722 1034 "5\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291722 1111 #uuid "56c023cb-ff0e-547e-8dbf-4804a1d42a97" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291723 1034 "\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{5}x)+C" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291723 1111 #uuid "496787cf-20ba-589f-bc48-a8f4411b8f02" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291724 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x)+C" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291724 1111 #uuid "28379061-67bd-5ac5-b4a6-b9761fbf6c90" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291725 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{5})+C" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291725 1111 #uuid "b6d2cb98-0809-5a37-ad14-29d9d43efd94" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291726 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291727 13194139534491 true] [17592186291726 1089 "q-346451" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291726 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534491 true] [17592186291726 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291726 1113 #uuid "e5f9130a-300a-596a-99eb-3945ea847a84" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291726 1145 "This integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{2}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1/3}\\frac{1}{1+(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{\\pi }{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291727 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291728 13194139534491 true] [17592186291727 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534491 true] [17592186291727 1041 "field-1" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291727 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291728 13194139534491 true] [17592186291727 1110 #uuid "aadbb490-6fb4-5470-9fd1-82edbc4e8d0f" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291728 1034 "\\frac{\\pi}{6}" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291728 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291728 1111 #uuid "34c2111c-2cfb-58ce-b087-b6d80745941d" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291729 1017 #edb/ref 17592186291730 13194139534491 true] [17592186291729 1089 "q-49546" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291729 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534491 true] [17592186291729 1100 "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}.$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291729 1113 #uuid "b6c3a048-1e47-59de-8a45-c489c544f459" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291729 1145 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}}\\, & ={\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{25\\cdot (1-{x}^{2}/25)}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}/25}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(\\frac{x}{5})}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\frac{x}{5}.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=5\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{5}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\sqrt{25-{x}^{2}}} & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-5/2}^{5/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(x/5)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}{\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (5\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1/2}^{1/2}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1/2}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291731 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291732 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291733 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291734 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291735 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1041 "selection" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291733 13194139534491 true] [17592186291730 1110 #uuid "6d4aa951-af9b-5825-9a3d-c4e6a9a0a712" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291731 1034 "\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" 13194139534491 true] [17592186291731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534491 true] [17592186291731 1111 #uuid "3fb3e6b9-359d-527e-b381-b4210d9e007d" 13194139534491 tr